---
/**
 * The landing page's credits: where SCCharts comes from, and that this guide is independent.
 */
---

<section class="sc-credits not-content" aria-labelledby="sc-credits-title">
	<h2 id="sc-credits-title" class="sc-landing-h2">Credits</h2>
	<div class="sc-credits__body">
		<p>
			SCCharts was created by the Real-Time and Embedded Systems group at Kiel University as part of the{' '}
			<a href="https://github.com/kieler">KIELER project</a>. It builds on Harel’s statecharts and on synchronous
			languages such as Esterel. The{' '}
			<a href="https://rtsys.informatik.uni-kiel.de/~biblio/downloads/papers/pldi14.pdf">PLDI 2014 paper</a> introduced
			it, and the <a href="https://github.com/kieler/semantics/wiki">KIELER wiki</a> is its reference documentation.
		</p>
		<p>
			This guide is an independent project, not part of KIELER or Kiel University. Its examples are checked against
			KIELER’s own compiler, tick for tick, so they behave here as they do in KIELER; where KIELER has a bug the guide
			does not copy, the example says so (<a href="/reference/about/">how this guide is checked</a>).
		</p>
	</div>
</section>

<style>
	.sc-credits {
		display: grid;
		gap: 1rem 3rem;
		padding-block: 3rem 1rem;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--c-rule);
	}
	.sc-credits__body {
		max-width: var(--measure);
		color: var(--c-muted);
		font-size: var(--text-sm);
		line-height: 1.6;
	}
	.sc-credits__body p + p {
		margin-top: 0.75rem;
	}
	.sc-credits__body a {
		color: var(--c-accent);
		text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
	}
	@media (min-width: 72rem) {
		.sc-credits {
			grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 20rem) minmax(0, 1fr);
		}
	}
</style>
